---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import Examples from '../../components/Examples.astro';
const faqs=[
{q:"How many 12x24 tiles do I need for 100 square feet?",a:"A nominal 12 × 24 inch tile covers 2 square feet. A 100 sq ft area needs 50 tiles before allowance, or 55 with 10% extra. If your selected product has 8 tiles per box, buy 7 boxes (56 tiles). Check the actual product dimensions and carton coverage."},
{q:"How do I calculate how many boxes of tile I need?",a:"Divide the area including your allowance by the area of one tile, round up to whole tiles, then divide by the actual tiles per box and round up to whole boxes. Box quantities vary by product; this calculator lets you enter the number on your carton."},
{q:"How much extra tile should I buy?",a:"The default 10% is a planning allowance, not a guarantee. Cuts, breakage, pattern and spare tiles can change the amount. Enter the allowance agreed with your installer, from 0 to 100%."},
{q:"Does this calculator include grout or installation labor?",a:"No. It estimates tile quantities and optional material cost from whole boxes. Grout, adhesive, delivery, tax and labor are excluded. Grout quantities require joint width, depth and the product manufacturer's coverage information."}
];
const related=[
{href:"/construction/square-footage-calculator",icon:"📏",title:"Square Footage",desc:"Calculate area for any space"},
{href:"/construction/concrete-calculator",icon:"🧱",title:"Concrete Calculator",desc:"Estimate concrete for slabs"},
{href:"/construction/paint-calculator",icon:"🎨",title:"Paint Calculator",desc:"How much paint you need"},
{href:"/math/percentage-calculator",icon:"%",title:"Percentage Calculator",desc:"Percent of a number"},
{href:"/converters/unit-converter",icon:"📏",title:"Unit Converter",desc:"Length, weight & temp"},
{href:"/math/fraction-calculator",icon:"½",title:"Fraction Calculator",desc:"Work with fractions"}
];
---
<CalculatorLayout title="Tile Calculator: Tiles, Boxes & Material Cost" h1="Tile Calculator" description="Calculate tiles and whole boxes for floors, walls or backsplashes. Enter tile size, tiles per box and waste; estimate material cost with 12x24 examples." subtitle="Estimate tiles, whole boxes and optional material cost for a rectangular floor, wall or backsplash." category="Construction" categoryHref="/construction" appCategory="UtilitiesApplication" faqs={faqs} relatedTools={related}>
<div slot="calculator">
<Examples examples={[
{label: '100 sq ft with 12 × 24 in tiles', values: {'tc-area-len':10,'tc-area-wid':10,'tc-tile-len':12,'tc-tile-wid':24,'tc-waste':10,'tc-per-box':8,'tc-price':''}},
{label: '8 × 2 ft backsplash, 3 × 6 in tiles', values: {'tc-area-len':8,'tc-area-wid':2,'tc-tile-len':3,'tc-tile-wid':6,'tc-waste':15,'tc-per-box':40,'tc-price':''}}
]} />
<div class="calc-grid">
<div>
<div class="input-row">
<div class="field"><label for="tc-area-len">Area length</label><div class="input-affix has-suffix"><input type="number" id="tc-area-len" value="10" step="any" /><span class="suffix">ft</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="tc-area-wid">Area width</label><div class="input-affix has-suffix"><input type="number" id="tc-area-wid" value="10" step="any" /><span class="suffix">ft</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="input-row">
<div class="field"><label for="tc-tile-len">Tile length</label><div class="input-affix has-suffix"><input type="number" id="tc-tile-len" value="12" step="any" /><span class="suffix">in</span></div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="tc-tile-wid">Tile width</label><div class="input-affix has-suffix"><input type="number" id="tc-tile-wid" value="12" step="any" /><span class="suffix">in</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="field"><label for="tc-waste">Extra tile allowance (%)</label><input type="number" id="tc-waste" value="10" min="0" max="100" step="any" /><div class="hint">Allow for cuts, breakage and spares. Adjust for your layout.</div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="tc-per-box">Tiles per box</label><input type="number" id="tc-per-box" value="10" min="1" step="1" /><div class="hint">Use the actual piece count printed on your product's box.</div></div>
<div class="field"><label for="tc-price">Price per box (USD, optional)</label><input type="number" id="tc-price" min="0" step="any" placeholder="Your supplier quote" /></div>
</div>
<div class="result-panel">
<div class="result-main"><div class="result-label">Tiles Needed</div><div class="result-value" id="tc-tiles">—</div><div class="result-sub" id="tc-sub">including 10% waste</div></div>
<div class="result-rows" id="tc-rows"></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<script>
import { tileEstimate } from '../../lib/materials.js';
(function(){
const ids=['tc-area-len','tc-area-wid','tc-tile-len','tc-tile-wid','tc-waste','tc-per-box','tc-price'];
function row(l,v){return '<div class="result-row"><span class="rr-label">'+l+'</span><span class="rr-value">'+v+'</span></div>';}
function calc(){
const values=ids.map(id=>document.getElementById(id).value.trim());
const r=tileEstimate(...values.slice(0,6).map(v=>v===''?NaN:Number(v)),values[6]===''?null:Number(values[6]));
if(!r){document.getElementById('tc-tiles').textContent='—';document.getElementById('tc-sub').textContent='Enter positive dimensions, a whole box count and allowance from 0 to 100%';document.getElementById('tc-rows').innerHTML='';return;}
document.getElementById('tc-tiles').textContent=r.tiles+' tiles';
document.getElementById('tc-sub').textContent=r.boxes+' whole boxes · '+values[4]+'% allowance';
document.getElementById('tc-rows').innerHTML=row('Surface area',r.area.toFixed(2)+' sq ft')+row('Area including allowance',r.orderArea.toFixed(2)+' sq ft')+row('Tiles before allowance',r.baseTiles)+row('Tiles to cover area + allowance',r.tiles)+row('Whole boxes to buy',r.boxes)+row('Tiles purchased in boxes',r.purchased)+row('Tiles above calculated requirement',r.purchased-r.tiles)+(r.cost===null?'':row('Tile material cost','$'+r.cost.toFixed(2)));
}
ids.forEach(id=>document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input',calc));calc();
})();
</script>
<section class="content-section">
<h2>How to calculate tiles and boxes</h2>
<div class="formula-box">Surface area = Length (ft) × Width (ft)<br>Tile area = Tile length (in) × Tile width (in) ÷ 144<br>Tiles = round up [Surface area × (1 + Allowance ÷ 100) ÷ Tile area]<br>Boxes = round up (Tiles ÷ Tiles per box)</div>
<p>Measure the area to cover, then use the dimensions and piece count for the tile you plan to buy. The optional cost multiplies <strong>whole boxes</strong> by your price per box. It does not use a national price estimate.</p>
<h2>12x24 tile calculator example: a 100 sq ft floor</h2>
<p>A 10 × 10 ft floor has 100 sq ft of area. A nominal 12 × 24 inch tile covers 2 sq ft, so the floor needs 50 tiles before cuts. With a 10% allowance, 110 ÷ 2 = <strong>55 tiles</strong>. With an example pack of 8 tiles, round 55 ÷ 8 up to <strong>7 boxes</strong>, providing 56 tiles. The example button loads these inputs; replace the pack size with your product's label.</p>
<h2>Backsplash tile calculator example</h2>
<p>An 8 ft long, 2 ft high backsplash covers 16 sq ft. A 3 × 6 inch tile covers 0.125 sq ft. Including 15% extra gives 18.4 ÷ 0.125 = 147.2, rounded to <strong>148 tiles</strong>. An example box of 40 tiles means 4 boxes, or 160 tiles. For several sections, combine their measured areas before rounding the final order.</p>
<h2>Tile area by nominal size</h2>
<table class="ref-table"><thead><tr><th>Tile size</th><th>Area per tile</th><th>Tiles for 100 sq ft + 10%</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>3 × 6 in</td><td>0.125 sq ft</td><td>880</td></tr>
<tr><td>12 × 12 in</td><td>1 sq ft</td><td>110</td></tr>
<tr><td>12 × 24 in</td><td>2 sq ft</td><td>55</td></tr>
<tr><td>18 × 18 in</td><td>2.25 sq ft</td><td>49</td></tr>
<tr><td>24 × 24 in</td><td>4 sq ft</td><td>28</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Check the carton and layout before ordering</h2>
<p>Box contents are product-specific. For example, this <a href="https://www.homedepot.com/catalog/pdfImages/3e/3e604f2d-eba8-40cf-93bc-48de440622da.pdf">tile manufacturer's carton planning guide hosted by The Home Depot</a> uses its own carton coverage and includes 10% overage. Do not transfer one product's box quantity to another tile.</p>
<p>This area-based estimate does not plan individual cuts, account for grout joints or optimize a diagonal pattern. Actual dimensions can differ from nominal sizes; compare against the carton coverage and confirm the layout with your installer. Mosaic sheets should be entered using sheet dimensions and sheets per box. Grout and adhesive are separate estimates.</p>
<p>Use the <a href="/construction/square-footage-calculator">square footage calculator</a> to measure your surfaces, or plan the room's walls with the <a href="/construction/paint-calculator">paint calculator for two coats</a>.</p>
</section>
</CalculatorLayout>
